  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "caller-mapping",
      "claim": "requestCaller in internal/api maps every principal producer to a core.Caller where the principal is built: human and service owners to their ID, kind and project; system-owned keys to system:<id>; external keys to external:<project>/<key>; the static admin key to gateway:admin; unauthenticated local requests to core.LocalCaller; gateway-internal calls to an anonymous caller. iam.CallerPrincipalID turns reserved and anonymous callers back into today's shared-only resolution, and system: callers into the system principal.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/caller.go; go/internal/iam/caller.go; table tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scopes-identical",
      "claim": "Provider-instance cache keys and catalog keys produce the same scope strings as before for every producer, including a system-owned key in two projects; a test compares the new caller with the principal iam.ResolveAPIKey builds through the pre-slice resolvers, including Copilot bindings.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api and go/internal/providers scope tests; go/internal/iam caller test"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "governance-identical",
      "claim": "Key governance moved to router.Governance in the request context, set by internal/api from the principal: hidden routes still answer 404 and models outside a key allowlist 403 on every request surface, routes-only, key and project allowlists, and project and key names on failover telemetry are unchanged; tests pin each and fail when broken.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/router/governance.go and governance_test.go; go/internal/api/governance.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "budgets",
      "claim": "internal/providers and internal/router no longer reference config.Principal: the coupling budgets move from 29 to 0 (providers), 26 to 0 (router) and 4 to 0 (api/transport_mode.go), with iam and config.Get counts unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/architecture/boundary_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens; every commit compiles with its tests; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head and go vet on each commit"
      }
    }
  ],
